\ login.fam — a user in: a name and a password from the input, checked
\ against /etc/passwd (lines of name:password:user:group:home:shell; the
\ password kept hashed, crypto/passwd.fam); the process then that user's
\ (/proc/self/user), in its home, running its shell, and ends when the
\ shell does.  It must start as root.  A password still kept in plain
\ text is hashed in its place once it is used.
\ uses: crypto/sha512.fam crypto/passwd.fam
: nm variable ;  : pw variable ;  : rb variable ;  : t variable ;  : st variable ;  : nf variable ;

\ rdl ( buf -- n | -1 )  a line of the input, NUL-ended; -1 at its end.
: rdl
rb !  0 lit
begin
	getc dup 0< if drop dup 0= if drop FFFFFFFF lit then 1 lit else
	dup A lit = if drop 1 lit else
	over 7E lit u< if over rb @ + c! 1 lit + else drop then 0 lit
	then then
until
dup 0< 0= if 0 lit over rb @ + c! then ;

\ found? ( -- ok )  the name's line found and the password its own; a
\ plain one hashed in its place (its fields read again after).
: found?
nm @ c@ 0= if 0 lit else
	nm @ pwfind if
		pw @ 1 lit pwfld pwok dup if
			1 lit pwfld pwp5? 0= if
				pw @ nf @ pwmake  nm @ nf @ pwset drop  nm @ pwfind drop
			then
		then
	else 0 lit then
then ;

: put  \ ( path s1 s2 -- )  path written with s1, a space, s2
t @ rot scpy 20 lit over c! 1 lit + swap scpy 0 lit swap c!
1 lit open dup 0< 0= if dup t @ dup strlen write drop close drop else drop then ;

80 lit alloc nm !  80 lit alloc pw !  100 lit alloc t !  100 lit alloc nf !
begin
	"login: " puts nm @ rdl 0< if bye then
	"password: " puts pw @ pwget drop
	found? if
		"/proc/self/user" 2 lit pwfld 3 lit pwfld put
		"/proc/self/cwd" 1 lit open dup 0< 0= if dup 4 lit pwfld dup strlen write drop close drop else drop then
		5 lit pwfld spawn dup 0< if "login: no shell" puts 0A lit putc drop else st wait drop then
		bye
	then
	"login incorrect" puts 0A lit putc
0 lit until
